@ywang96 Thanks to your review. The reason behind doing this is that we can adjust parallelism of target model without affected by draft model. The draft model is often a dense model with tensor parallelism and the target model has many architectures with different parallelism. For example, moe model with ep+dp `docs/serving/expert_parallel_deployment.md`. 
@tomasruizt gives one another reason. TP > 1 is for large model, memory bound. TP = 1 for smaller one.
And I think it's an open method for developer to obtain different latency or throughput behavior using `draft_tensor_parallel_size` and other draft model parallelism.
